{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.InformationSpeedOfLight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.InformationSpeedOfLight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight_mul_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight_mul_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.lean#L69-L79","doc":"**The speed of light equals the ratio `q⁻¹ / ℏ_q`**, stated division-free\nas `c_q · ℏ_q = q⁻¹` with `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` (the R[h] pattern).\n\n`1/(q−1) = q⁻¹ · q/(q−1) = q⁻¹/((q−1)/q) = q⁻¹/(1 − q⁻¹)`, i.e.\n`c_q · (1 − q⁻¹) = q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.isUnit_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.isUnit_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.lean#L57-L67","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` is a unit, namely\n`↑(d · q⁻¹)` with `↑d = q − 1`.  Consequently the narrative's quotient\npresentation `c_q = q⁻¹ / ℏ_q` is equivalent to the multiplicative form\nproved below — de-specialising to `CommRing` loses nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight_mul","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.lean#L51-L55","doc":"**Defining relation, division-free**: `c_q · (q − 1) = 1`, where\n`↑d = q − 1`. This is the whole content of `c_q = 1/(q − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.lean#L38-L49","doc":"**Speed of light** at substrate parameter q.\n\nc_q := 1 / (q - 1)\n\nThe ratio of spatial to temporal information transfer within\na light cone: spatial coupling weight q⁻¹ divided by temporal\ncoupling weight ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹.\n\n§7c: the temporal weight `q − 1` is carried as the unit `d : kˣ`, so\n`c_q` is the ring element `↑d⁻¹` — no field structure is required. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:information-speed-of-light","label":"def:information-speed-of-light","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}